<chapter id="id0a1b2c03-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000003" identifier="/us/usc/t99/ch1"><num value="1">Chapter 1—</num><heading>Widgets</heading>
<section id="id0a1b2c04-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000004" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1"><num value="1">§ 1.</num><heading>Definitions</heading>
<chapeau id="id0a1b2c05-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000005">In this invented chapter—</chapeau>
<paragraph id="id0a1b2c06-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000006" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/1"><num value="1">(1)</num><content id="id0a1b2c07-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000007">the term “widget” means a small device<ref class="footnoteRef" idref="id0a1b2c08-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000008">1</ref><note type="footnote" id="id0a1b2c08-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000008"><num>1</num> So in original.</note>; and</content></paragraph>
<paragraph id="id0a1b2c09-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000009" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s1/2"><num value="2">(2)</num><content id="id0a1b2c0a-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000a">the term “gadget” has the meaning given in <ref href="/us/usc/t99/s2">section 2 of this title</ref>.</content></paragraph>
<sourceCredit id="id0a1b2c0b-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000b">(Invented act, § 1.)</sourceCredit>
<notes type="uscNote" id="id0a1b2c0c-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000c">
<note role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes" id="id0a1b2c0d-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000d"><heading><b>Editorial Notes</b></heading></note>
<note topic="amendments" id="id0a1b2c0e-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000e"><heading>Amendments</heading><p id="id0a1b2c0f-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f00000f">2099—Par. (2) added.</p></note>
</notes>
</section>
<section id="id0a1b2c10-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000010" identifier="/us/usc/t99/s2"><num value="2">§ 2.</num><heading>Gadgets</heading><content id="id0a1b2c11-ac5f-11f1-b305-0d0e0f000011">A gadget is a widget of any size.</content></section>
</chapter>
